# NOT ready to be enabled — this key needs a bcrypt hash and nothing produces one yet.
#
# docker-compose.yaml passes this straight into wg-easy's PASSWORD_HASH, and v14 checks it
# with `bcrypt.compareSync(password, PASSWORD_HASH)` (verified in the image at
# /app/lib/Server.js:54). So a random hex secret here would make login impossible, and the
# fixed placeholder it used to carry was no better.
#
# Left empty rather than filled with something that only looks functional. Be aware of what
# empty means: `requiresPassword = !!PASSWORD_HASH`, so the web UI comes up with no
# password at all. That is acceptable only because this application is not offered yet.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
